+// Online play through Nextendo Network (https://nextendo.network), a community server for Switch games: the host's side of it.
+// Off unless DM_NEXTENDO=1 and the game is one this host knows how to take online (Super Smash Bros. Ultimate 13.0.5 so far). Off, every
+// network call keeps its offline answer (hle_net.c, hle_account.c), so no other game changes.
+//
+// The pieces (docs/nextendo.md has the whole picture):
+//   account   a Nextendo account signed in with OAuth 2.0 (authorization code + PKCE, public client) in an in-app browser sheet whose redirect
+//             a listener on 127.0.0.1 catches; the refresh token in the Keychain; at need, GET /api/nex-token for the game's NEX login token
+//             (net_nextendo_apple.m)
+//   id token  the network service account ID token the game hands its NEX login: a JWT shaped like Nintendo BaaS's, carrying the Nextendo
+//             PID as "sub" and the NEX login token as "nnex", which is what Nextendo's game server checks
+//   names     every *.nintendo.net name the game resolves is Nextendo's: nncs2-* (Pia's second NAT check server) is their NAT check, every
+//             other one their game server. Nothing else resolves
+//   NEX       the game's NEX client is pointed at a stand-in address (NX_BRIDGE_IP, observation gate OBS_NEX_LOGIN on its login job) where it
+//             speaks its WebSocket without TLS; a TCP connection there is a bridge that carries it to Nextendo's game server in TLS, the
+//             server's key pinned (Network.framework). Pia's UDP goes straight to the other players, as on a console
+//
+// Switches (environment; the launcher's "Nextendo online" row sets the first):
+//   DM_NEXTENDO=1               go online through Nextendo
+//   DM_NEXTENDO_CLIENT_ID       the OAuth client ID of your own application at nextendo.network/developers (default: NX_CLIENT_ID_DEFAULT)
+//   DM_NEXTENDO_REDIRECT_PORT   the loopback port of its registered redirect, http://127.0.0.1:<port>/callback (default 47823)
+//   DM_NEXTENDO_API             the account API (default https://nextendo.network)
+//   DM_NEXTENDO_SERVER          the game server, a dotted IPv4 address[:port] (default NX_SERVER_DEFAULT:443)
+//   DM_NEXTENDO_NAT             the NAT check server, a dotted IPv4 address (default NX_NAT_DEFAULT)
+//   DM_NEXTENDO_PIN             the game server's public key: SHA-256 of its SubjectPublicKeyInfo, 64 hex digits (default NX_PIN_DEFAULT)
+//   DM_NEXTENDO_LOG=1           log every socket, name and bridge event (the PID, tokens and codes are never logged)
+//   DM_NEXTENDO_SIGNOUT=1       forget the stored account at start (the next online step asks to sign in again)
+#pragma once
+#include <stddef.h>
+#include <stdint.h>
+
+// Your application's client ID (nextendo.network → Developers → New application: public, PKCE, redirect http://127.0.0.1:47823/callback,
+// scopes identity and game.matchmaking). This is the fork's own application; DM_NEXTENDO_CLIENT_ID names another.
+#define NX_CLIENT_ID_DEFAULT "nxc_iCNSyIfLdS5o"
+// Nextendo's addresses as Super Mario Bros. 35 Recomp ships them (github.com/sm35recomp/sm35recomp, recomp/runtime/net/netcfg.h). Not yet
+// confirmed for Super Smash Bros. Ultimate: ask Nextendo, and override with the switches above if theirs differ.
+#define NX_SERVER_DEFAULT "51.178.29.194"
+#define NX_NAT_DEFAULT "164.132.111.120"
